+---
+id: dl-004-applymergepatch-is-non-mutating-and-rejects-non-json-input
+type: decision-log
+title: "applyMergePatch is non-mutating and rejects non-JSON input"
+status: pending
+---
+
+# Decision — applyMergePatch is non-mutating and rejects non-JSON input
+
+## Context
+RFC 7386 gives a recursive algorithm that mutates the target. The library's `applyPatch` never mutates
+its inputs and rejects values that are not JSON (dl-002, dl-003).
+
+## Decision
+- `applyMergePatch` builds a new value and clones non-object patch values, so the result shares nothing
+  with either input.
+- Target and patch must be JSON values (same check as `applyPatch`); otherwise it throws an `Error`.
+- Only own members of the target are merged, and members are set without the `__proto__` setter.
+- Arrays are replaced whole, and `null` inside arrays is kept, as the RFC specifies.
+
+## Consequences
+Consistent behaviour across the library's patch functions. A patch cannot set a member to `null`
+(inherent to RFC 7386). Input validation costs one extra walk of each input.
